<Doc lang={lang} page="blocks" current="Calibration" title="Calibration"
  description="The Calibration block of FLOAT: the session and the frames it takes, the inventory, master dark, flat and bias, hot and defective pixels, flats from another night, several sessions, with the settings and limits.">

  <p class="kicker">Block</p>
  <h1>Calibration</h1>
  <p class="meta">FLOAT 0.2.0 · beta of {release.date.en}</p>

  <dl class="inshort"><div><dt>What it does</dt><dd>It cleans every raw frame with the darks and flats: it takes off the camera’s own signal, evens out the vignetting and the dust shadows, and repairs the hot and dead pixels.</dd></div><div><dt>What it shows</dt><dd>In Inspect, the master dark and the master flat, with the flat minimum, the share of excluded pixels and the sky noise; in the Report, the calibration frames used and these figures.</dd></div><div><dt>What can be set</dt><dd>Usually nothing: the defaults suit. Flat scale (about 40 px) for flats borrowed from another night, and the Hot pixel threshold if too many pixels are excluded.</dd></div></dl>

